WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.270
- She's no stranger to
blockbusters herself.

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:04.910
You've seen her in dozens over
the years from "Halloween"

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:06.840
to my personal favorite, "Knives Out."

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.840
Her new podcast, "Letters
From Camp," is out now.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.372
Let's dial in with
Jamie Lee Curtis, y'all.

00:00:12.372 --> 00:00:13.384
(audience applauds)

00:00:13.384 --> 00:00:16.384
(gentle jazz music)

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:19.830
Hi! Oh, wait, there she is.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.120
- Hi.
- Oh, hi. Oh, my gosh.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.520
Your whole look is so cool.
- Oh, I'm right here.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:24.763
- Yes, can you hear me?

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:26.950
- I can, what do you mean?

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:28.750
What is so cool? You're cool.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:31.860
- No, your whole vibe. I
love your glasses, the hair.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:34.530
Your whole vibe is so cool.
- Well, I'm an old woman.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:36.310
We wear glasses.
- Whatever, you look rock

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:37.990
and roll right now, I would love that.

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:40.390
So wait, are you getting
used to all this Skyping

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:41.223
and Zooming we do now?

00:00:41.223 --> 00:00:42.970
I had never even heard
of Zoom before this.

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:43.910
- And neither had I.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:48.020
And the truth of the matter
is that I'm a technical girl.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:51.380
I can work my way around some
sort of technology, lighting.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:52.620
Obviously, I'm a photographer,

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:54.300
so I know kind of where to put the light.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.700
But the truth of the matter is my husband

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.970
and I had never done any
sort of Zoom or FaceTime.

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:03.810
The word FaceTime to me, always
like, oh, FaceTime? Go away.

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:05.140
I don't wanna look at.

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:09.000
And my daughter, Annie, and her husband...

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:11.569
My daughter got married.

00:01:11.569 --> 00:01:13.420
- Oh, that's so exciting.
- And so they just had

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:15.557
a year's anniversary, thank you.

00:01:15.557 --> 00:01:19.830
But they taught us how to
Zoom for the first time.

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:21.030
- Well, speaking of tech,

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:24.210
sometimes it gets
(chuckles) the better of us.

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:27.100
Like with your "Knives
Out" costar, Chris Evans.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:27.933
What happened here?

00:01:27.933 --> 00:01:30.060
Do you know what happened (laughs)

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:31.450
with that whole thing that-

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:33.130
- Well, I think we...
(audience laughs)

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:34.998
Well, that whole thing, exactly.

00:01:34.998 --> 00:01:37.990
(Kelly laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:39.385
- I didn't know how to word it.

00:01:39.385 --> 00:01:41.880
- Hey, I didn't say it so long as you did.

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:43.310
Look, I'm sweating already. (laughs)

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:45.590
- I know, I just was
like, was it an accident?

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:47.350
And then all of a sudden,
I love that he turned it

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:49.790
into like, now that
I've got your attention.

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:51.210
That was awesome.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:55.590
- So my question is this, he's so smart

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:59.961
and such a unbelievably
beautiful human being,

00:01:59.961 --> 00:02:04.090
I'm wondering if it was even planned.

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:05.520
- Oh, he's so clever.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.250
I kinda think it was planned
just 'cause he was trying

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:08.952
to get people to vote, you know?

00:02:08.952 --> 00:02:09.785
- Right.
- And he was like,

00:02:09.785 --> 00:02:10.798
"Now that I have your attention."

00:02:10.798 --> 00:02:12.860
- And you know... (laughs)

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:13.730
But you know what I mean?

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:15.720
I could've made some sort of joke

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:19.230
and say he took after his
movie father, Don Johnson,

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:22.850
or I could be also like...
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:25.190
'Cause I'm really, really close friends

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:26.140
with Melanie Griffith.

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:28.220
She's one of my best friends
and has been forever.

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:30.580
And she was married to him twice,

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:32.980
so.
- Twice? I didn't know that.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:33.813
- Yeah.

00:02:33.813 --> 00:02:35.550
- I guess she didn't know
the first time. (laughs)

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:36.383
That's awesome.

00:02:36.383 --> 00:02:38.750
You have a new project
called My Hand In Yours.

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:40.250
So what is it, and what inspired it?

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:41.730
I think I have some stuff here.

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:43.380
- Yes you do. Thank you for mentioning it.

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:46.670
- Yeah.
- So I'm 61 years old,

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:49.710
and for a long time, when
anyone has ever been sad

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:52.590
or going through a hard time,
I will always write a note

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:55.520
and say at the end of
it, "My hand in yours,"

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:57.900
as if to say to them,
I'm not there with you,

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:00.840
but imagine what it would feel
like if my hand was in yours.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:05.090
And then about a year ago, I
realized that I could turn it

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:07.950
into something to benefit
Children's Hospital Los Angeles.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:09.810
And I went to a sculptor friend of mine.

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:11.880
And I think I saw that
you have the sculpture.

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:12.713
- [Kelly] Yes!

00:03:12.713 --> 00:03:16.820
- And I asked her if she would
make a small hand sculpture

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:17.848
of two hands holding.

00:03:17.848 --> 00:03:19.170
- [Kelly] It's so beautiful.

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:21.200
- And do you see it there?

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.033
- Yes, it's in my hand.
- Can you see it

00:03:22.033 --> 00:03:22.866
on your thing?

00:03:22.866 --> 00:03:23.699
Yes, it's right there.

00:03:23.699 --> 00:03:25.810
And it fits in the palm of your hand.

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:29.050
And I decided to start a store.

00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:31.760
So at 61 years old, I've started a store.

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:35.670
100% of all of the sales
of all of the objects,

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:38.050
for instance, I'm wearing
a necklace right now.

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:43.050
So it's a small hand pendant
on a beautiful silver chain.

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:46.980
- Yes.
- And there are other objects.

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:50.100
And all of the sale of all of these items

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:52.620
goes toward Children's
Hospital Los Angeles.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:57.060
And all of the artists
donated all of their time.

00:03:57.060 --> 00:04:00.960
And we are adding notebooks,
and blankets, and pillows.

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:04.440
And so it's a way for
people to send to loved ones

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:08.380
at this time where it's so,
so difficult for everyone

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:10.280
to feel that connection.

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:12.260
And particularly because of the pandemic,

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:14.210
which, of course, I wasn't anticipating

00:04:14.210 --> 00:04:16.100
when I invented this whole idea.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:16.933
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:16.933 --> 00:04:18.870
- It just happens to have
come out right at a time

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:22.120
when people need love and
comfort more than ever.

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:23.040
- Yeah, I don't believe in accidents.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:23.873
- [Jamie] So that's what I mean it to be.

00:04:23.873 --> 00:04:24.706
- Yeah, I don't believe in accidents.

00:04:24.706 --> 00:04:26.720
I think that it's a really cool thing

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:28.140
that it happened to come
out right in this time

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:31.430
when people do need it more
now than ever with connection.

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:32.263
But you've-

00:04:32.263 --> 00:04:34.960
- And you can send a note with it.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:39.960
And even the little medallion,
which you have there, is $12.

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:43.180
And again, 100% of all of the sales

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:45.110
goes right to Children's Hospital.

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:46.670
And-
- So great.

00:04:46.670 --> 00:04:47.830
- People are responding.

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:50.780
And it's really heartwarming at this time

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:54.500
where everybody feels so
divided, so complicated,

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:57.470
so conflicted about so many things

00:04:57.470 --> 00:04:59.880
that you can cross all boundaries

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:02.530
and reach out and give a gift to someone,

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:06.340
and say, I'm thinking of
you, my hand in yours,

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:08.050
and that I think my hand in yours

00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:10.157
is how we're gonna heal
this country right now.

00:05:10.157 --> 00:05:11.812
- That's so beautifully,

00:05:11.812 --> 00:05:13.040
beautifully said.
- It's a hard time.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:13.930
- Yeah.

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:16.210
Well, you've also been
working on a podcast

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:17.980
during the pandemic, so what's that about?

00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:18.813
- I did.

00:05:18.813 --> 00:05:21.700
So weirdly enough, this is a true story,

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:25.690
my goddaughter, who's now 26,
wrote me a letter from camp

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:27.900
when she was 12 and never sent it.

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:31.380
And her mother sent it
to me last November.

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:32.780
And it was sealed in an envelope

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:34.750
with that kind of 12-year-old handwriting.

00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:38.277
And it was a 12-year-old's
letter from camp saying,

00:05:38.277 --> 00:05:41.340
"Dear godmother, Jamie, I made a mistake.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:43.040
I did something stupid."

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:47.177
And ultimately, what happened
is that I said to her,

00:05:47.177 --> 00:05:49.300
"This should be a TV show or something."

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:53.240
And it turned out to be a
scripted podcast for Audible,

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:57.070
very funny, a comedy
called "Letters From Camp."

00:05:57.070 --> 00:06:00.190
And it is a hilarious show.

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:03.280
It stars a young actress
named Sunny Sandler.

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:05.580
My godson, Jake Gyllenhaal, is in it,

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:09.070
Edi Patterson, Kirby
Howell-Baptiste, and yours truly.

00:06:09.070 --> 00:06:11.650
I play the camp director, natch.

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:15.660
And it's really fun,
funny, and it's nostalgic.

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:18.160
And it was a way, again, with COVID

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:21.410
for kids to be able to go back to camp

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:23.200
because, of course, so
many kids didn't get

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:24.350
to go to camp this summer.

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:28.120
- Well, speaking of kiddos,
congrats on 35 years of marriage

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:30.537
with the very funny Christopher Guest.

00:06:30.537 --> 00:06:31.370
(audience applauds)
- Six.

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:33.054
- Oh, really?
- 36.

00:06:33.054 --> 00:06:34.500
I mean, but who's counting?

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:36.420
- Wow, I would be if it's that many.

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:38.604
Wait, so how did you meet?

00:06:38.604 --> 00:06:41.470
- (laughs) All right.

00:06:41.470 --> 00:06:43.100
I'll trying to figure out a really fast,

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:44.260
but it's a funny story.

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:45.943
So I was single.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:49.230
I was looking at "Rolling Stone" magazine,

00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:52.870
and I turned the page in 1984,

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:54.280
and there was a picture of three men

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:56.790
with their arms around
each other like dudes.

00:06:56.790 --> 00:06:59.317
And I said to my girlfriend, Debra Hill,

00:06:59.317 --> 00:07:01.490
"Oh, I'm gonna marry that guy."

00:07:01.490 --> 00:07:04.130
And I pointed to the guy on
the outside of the picture.

00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:07.380
And she said, "Oh, yeah, I tried
to put him in a movie once.

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:08.890
He's an actor. His name is Chris Guest."

00:07:08.890 --> 00:07:10.280
I was like, "Oh, I'm gonna marry him."

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:12.190
Never seen him in my life.

00:07:12.190 --> 00:07:13.023
- What?
- And she said,

00:07:13.023 --> 00:07:14.300
"He's with your agency."

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:17.070
Never saw him. Well, I never saw him.

00:07:17.070 --> 00:07:21.220
And so the next day, I called his agent

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:22.500
'cause that's what one does.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:24.927
And he picked up the phone and said,

00:07:24.927 --> 00:07:27.110
"I know all about it, Jamie. Chris Guest."

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:30.060
And I was like, "Ah, yeah,
I know. The guy's cute.

00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:31.560
Here's my number. I think he's cute.

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:32.420
Goodbye."

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:33.630
And then he never called me.

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:35.640
and I dated somebody
else for a couple months,

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:38.110
and then broke up with that person.

00:07:38.110 --> 00:07:39.750
Took that person to the airport.

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:42.080
Went from the airport,
picked up Melanie Griffith

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:44.550
and her then husband, Steve Bauer.

00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:47.770
And we went to Hugo's in
West Hollywood. I sat down.

00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:51.930
Two tables away was
Christopher facing me, swear.

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:54.533
And he looked at me and he went like this.

00:07:56.235 --> 00:07:57.068
(Kelly laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:07:57.068 --> 00:07:59.050
And then I looked at him and did the same.

00:07:59.050 --> 00:08:02.480
And then two minutes later, he
got up to leave or something,

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:05.433
and he stood there next to his
seat and he went like this.

00:08:08.350 --> 00:08:10.821
And then I went like.
(audience laughs)

00:08:10.821 --> 00:08:12.595
- (laughs) Hey again. (laughs)
- And then he left.

00:08:12.595 --> 00:08:17.230
But then he called me,
mm-hmm, the next day.

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:19.350
That was June 28th.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:21.230
He was leaving to do "Saturday Night Live"

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:23.193
for a year on August 8th.

00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:25.890
He left for a year.

00:08:25.890 --> 00:08:27.777
I was making the movie, "Perfect."

00:08:28.680 --> 00:08:31.140
We got engaged September 13th.

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:34.510
And we got married
December 18 of that year.

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:37.040
So we knew each other four months

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:40.066
and had never spent more
than three days together

00:08:40.066 --> 00:08:41.950
at a time.
- That's an insane story.

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:43.843
That's a movie right there.

00:08:43.843 --> 00:08:45.050
(Jamie laughs)
And are you talking

00:08:45.050 --> 00:08:47.030
about this magazine?
- Well, let me say this.

00:08:47.030 --> 00:08:47.863
It's my life.
- Is the magazine

00:08:47.863 --> 00:08:49.000
you're referring to?

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:51.180
- That's the, okay. Yes,
so show the picture.

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:52.950
- Oh, oh, I will.
- Okay.

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:54.288
So you're gonna find it.

00:08:54.288 --> 00:08:55.121
- I am.
- Okay, now you're gonna

00:08:55.121 --> 00:08:55.954
have to find it.

00:08:55.954 --> 00:08:56.883
- No, I'll find it.

00:08:56.883 --> 00:08:58.040
It's right here.
- It's a pic, okay there.

00:08:58.040 --> 00:08:59.340
It's so crazy.

00:08:59.340 --> 00:09:00.610
- [Kelly] Boom.

00:09:00.610 --> 00:09:02.120
- That's crazy.

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:03.880
- Boom.
- Okay, I literally saw

00:09:03.880 --> 00:09:07.680
the guy on the right, and I
said, "I'm gonna marry him,"

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:08.650
and I married him-

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:10.870
- I think that's so sweet.
- 36 years ago.

00:09:10.870 --> 00:09:12.810
- I love you so much.
- You know what?

00:09:12.810 --> 00:09:13.670
(Kelly chuckles)

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:15.060
And I love you.

00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:16.410
- (laughs) All right, y'all.

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:18.620
For more information
about My Hand In Yours,

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:19.560
go to our website.

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:22.730
Check out Jamie's new podcast,
"Letters From Camp," as well.

00:09:22.730 --> 00:09:25.400
And you can catch her next
year in "Halloween Kills,"

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:26.653
which I'm excited about.

